Acceptance criterion: If a student performs poorly on a topic test, the system must create a targeted intervention and update future priorities without disrupting an active study or mock-exam session.

## 5\. Learn module: video player, AI assistant, and notes

The Learn module should function as a single workspace rather than separate pages for videos, summaries, doubts, and notes.

### Required functionality

- Save playback progress and resume from the last watched timestamp.
- Organize videos by paper, subject, topic, and subtopic.
- Add timestamped bookmarks for formulas, derivations, and examples.
- Provide transcript search and jump-to-timestamp navigation when transcripts are available.
- Generate short summaries, detailed notes, formula sheets, and exam-oriented takeaways.
- Support contextual AI questions using the current video, timestamp, transcript, and linked notes.
- Save useful AI explanations directly into notes.
- Generate a topic test based on the full available lecture content.
- Handle missing transcripts and unsupported videos gracefully.
- Maintain a searchable history of doubts and saved explanations.
- Track actual watched segments rather than assuming that opening or playing a video means the topic is understood.

