## 20\. How to measure whether the improvements work

Measure learning efficiency and reliability rather than total time spent inside the app.

| Metric | What it tells you |
| --- | --- |
| Time to first study action | Whether the dashboard is easy to use |
| Planned-task completion rate | Whether the roadmap is realistic |
| First-attempt topic accuracy | Whether concepts are being understood |
| Repeat error rate | Whether targeted revision is effective |
| Retention on delayed quizzes | Whether knowledge persists |
| PYQ completion and accuracy | Whether preparation translates to exam-style problem solving |
| Mock performance trend | Whether exam readiness is improving |
| Schedule recovery rate | Whether missed tasks can be managed sustainably |
| Data-loss and scoring defect rate | Whether the app is reliable |
| Recommendation acceptance and usefulness | Whether the adaptive engine helps users |

Avoid treating app opens, watch time, streak length, or AI queries as evidence of learning on their own.

