## My final recommendation

If you only implement five improvements first, make them these:

1. Redesign the dashboard around the next best study action.
2. Build a personalized, adaptive planner that respects actual availability.
3. Connect learning, testing, mistake tracking, and revision into one continuous workflow.
4. Make the mock-exam simulator accurate, persistent, and reliable.
5. Build topic-level mastery tracking that explains weaknesses and recommends corrective action.

These five improvements will deliver substantially more value than adding more dashboard cards, animations, badges, or AI buttons.

The product's defining advantage should be that it understands not only what the student has completed, but also what the student can actually solve, what they are forgetting, and what they should study next.